+
+R17 review corrections keep the shared point parser's unit context explicit for
+midpoint lines, conics and all three spline creators, as well as endpoint
+references used by tangent arcs and blends. Numeric paper positions and bare
+coordinate strings therefore use the same paper-mm frame even when the source
+design displays inches. Named source expressions retain their authored units
+and resolve again without baking values into the stored drawing. The model
+route still supplies its original design-unit context.
+
+Rounded rectangles and dimensioned creators use a scratch Session for atomic
+publication. Adopting that changed, history-free scratch replaces only its
+current owner's redo branch, leaving the model and other drawings' redo steps
+available. Scratch-only owner provenance watches only redo owners relevant to
+its parent, with fixed keys rather than an edit log that grows with each new
+drawing. It survives bounded undo eviction and nested compound history clearing;
+adoption replaces every touched owner's branch even if another tab is open.
+An ordinary Session has no such watch map. A checkpoint restores matching
+provenance with its document and history, including across file.new. Failed
+commands restore precommand provenance; read-only resolution or tab switching
+leaves every redo branch available. A new compound edit ends the current
+drawing's redo branch, and failed creation or
+driving constraints publish no geometry or history. Original regression cases
+in the existing Drawing test module cover literal/expression unit context,
+foreign redo branches, one-step compound history and refusal after a nested
+line creator. Their execution status belongs to the exact-source validation
+receipt; these cases alone do not establish the full CI or editor acceptance.
